clear @s written_book
give @s written_book[written_book_content={title:"Little Command Book",author:"Command Forge",pages:[{"font":"minecraft:uniform","text":"How to type a command\n\n1. Press t to open chat.\n2. Type / first.\n3. Type the command.\n4. Press Enter.\n\nEsc closes chat."},{"font":"minecraft:uniform","text":"Tab = finish my word\n\nType part of a word and press Tab. Minecraft finishes it!\n\nPress Tab again to see more choices.\n\nIn /tp, Tab fills in the block you are looking at."},{"font":"minecraft:uniform","text":"Up arrow = last command\n\nIn the chat box, press the Up arrow. Your last command comes back.\n\nChange a word, press Enter. Done!"},{"font":"minecraft:uniform","text":"Big words\n\nCLI = command-line interface. You control a program by typing words, not clicking.\n\nREPL = Read, Evaluate, Print, Loop. You type, Minecraft reads it, runs it, prints an answer, and waits for more."},{"font":"minecraft:uniform","text":"Commands I know\n\n/say <words>\n/gamemode creative\n/give @s <item> <count>\n/clear @s <item>\n/tp @s X Y Z\n/help <command>"},{"font":"minecraft:uniform","text":"Names\n\nminecraft:cookie and cookie mean the same thing.\n\n@s means your player.\n\nX Y Z = east, up, south."},{"font":"minecraft:uniform","text":"Stuck?\n\n","extra":[{"font":"minecraft:uniform","text":"[Start this exercise over]","color":"red","click_event":{"action":"run_command","command":"trigger tut_btn set 3"}}]},{"font":"minecraft:uniform","text":"For teachers\n\n/function tut:___skip\n/function tut:___goto {sec:1,ex:3}\n/function tut:___reset_player\n/function tut:___reset_world\n\nRun one as a kid:\n/execute as Name run function tut:___skip"}]}]
